@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Enable Endpoint Command
  "CLI handler for mason enable: re-activate a disabled share endpoint."

  Provides:
    - cli.newEnableCommand @source("symbol:newEnableCommand")
    - cli.defaultEnableRun @source("symbol:defaultEnableRun")

  Consumes:
    - links.Service.Enable
    - cli.renderEndpoint
    - cli.shareStack
    - output.WriteJSON

  Invariants:
    - Human output MUST distinguish changed vs already-enabled no-ops
    - Quiet mode MUST emit no stdout on success
    - JSON output MUST use the stable endpointJSON shape under output.Success

  Scenario (happy-path): Enable endpoint
    Given Enable changes state
    When the command completes
    Then stdout reports Enabled <ref>

  Scenario (negative): Enable failure
    Given Enable returns an error
    When the command runs
    Then emitError renders the failure
